  "open_reviews": [
    "Pin 40 is unswitched USB VBUS with no on-board current limit or reverse blocking; 3 A target and top-side-only assembly require assembled-board qualification",
    "Hot-plug ringing at 20 V must be scoped at U4 to confirm the D5 clamp keeps VBUS below the 40 V regulator limit",
    "Inductive loads require an external driver and local suppression; 5 V 24BYJ48 example is not rated for higher PD voltages",
    "Carrier capacitance inrush and PD voltage transitions require measurements with representative sources",
    "Current PCB/assembly quote, MCU stock and 20-device allocation (docs/design.md)",
    "Measured USB performance; nonuniform connector/package fanouts (docs/usb-routing.md)",
    "Physical USB cable, overhang and locating-peg fit (docs/design.md)",
    "Pin 37 shutdown/restart, released EN voltage, back-power and loaded PD shutdown timing",
    "Power copper/contact temperature, source short-circuit behavior, backfeed and fixed 3.3 V load budget; reserve at least 100 mA from the negotiated input current",
    "Native USB ISP/recovery, open PD/CDC firmware integration, reset/detach handling and watchdog",
    "JLC IC/diode polarity and stencil review, provisional 0.125 mm stencil for the D5 exposed pad; supplier process approval pending, order quantity/attrition"
  ]
